  div style="font-size: 10px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; margin-top: 6px; padding-bottom: 2px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);"
    "Value & Send"
  div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-sm);"
    label style="width: 72px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: var(--font-size-sm); color: var(--text-secondary);"
      "Unit"
    input placeholder="e.g. dB, %" style="flex: 1 1 0%;" value="dB"
  div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-sm);"
    label style="width: 72px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: var(--font-size-sm); color: var(--text-secondary);"
      "Shown decimals"
    input type="number" placeholder="Auto" min="0" max="6" step="1" style="flex: 1 1 0%;" value="1"
  div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-sm);"
    label style="width: 72px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: var(--font-size-sm); color: var(--text-secondary);"
      "Send"
    select style="flex: 1 1 0%;" value="live"
      option value="live"
        "While dragging"
      option value="release"
        "On release only"
  div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-sm);"
    label style="width: 72px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: var(--font-size-sm); color: var(--text-secondary);"
      "Rate (ms)"
    input type="number" placeholder="100" min="0" step="10" style="flex: 1 1 0%;" value="20"
  div style="font-size: 10px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: -2px; margin-bottom: 4px;"
    "Rate is the shortest time between commands while dragging; 0 sends every movement."
    ""On release only" sends one command when you let go. Use it for devices that can't keep up with a stream of commands. Shown decimals affect the readout, not the value sent (a driver formats that)."
